  "explanation": {
    "event_selection": "The unified protocol uses only task-level object and zone search/approach actions, color observations, claims, pickup/drop operations, failure recovery releases, and delivery publication events needed to collect one box and deliver it to its matching colored zone. Low-level movement and obstacle events are omitted because collision_avoidance already protects motion, while unrelated reception and release notifications do not affect this robot's protocol state.",
    "transition_design": "object_search repeatedly enables search_object and enters a color-specific claim-attempt state only after the matching visible observation. Each claim attempt handles the corresponding received_claim event by abandoning that box. A successful claim immediately enables approach_object; not-visible observations return to color-specific search states, and reached observations permit pick_up_object. Pickup failure forces release of the claim. After pickup confirmation, only the matching zone branch is available; drop_object is enabled only after that zone is reached. Delivery failure resumes matching-zone search, while confirmation requires the matching publish_delivered event before the sole marked state delivery_complete.",
    "feedback_response": "No previous-run feedback was supplied."
  }
